  "check": "both counts transcribed; first preferences sum to 6,781 (ARK gives no valid poll; turnout \"reported to be 46%\"); at the second count Mussen, Kelly and Whitcroft were excluded together and 484 of their 2,132 papers were non-transferable; the quota of 3,391 is half the valid vote plus one, and Paul McKibben was elected as the higher of the two left",
  "notes": [
   "Poll on Wednesday 18 June 2003, after the SDLP councillor Hugh Carr resigned in April 2003. ARK gives only the year. The date is the one in the Electoral Office's result file name (newry_and_mourne_crotlieve_180603.pdf, on its archived Elections page headed \"Crotlieve DEA By-Election\"), and An Phoblacht (26 June 2003) reported the poll as \"last Wednesday\"; Newry and Mourne District Council's minutes record Carr's resignation (7 April 2003) and welcome the newly elected Paul McKibben (23 June 2003)."
